<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">French Second Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1848 CE – 1852 CE · capital Paris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short republic of 1848 that introduced universal male suffrage and abolished slavery, then elected the president who would overthrow it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The February Revolution of 1848 toppled the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/july-monarchy">July Monarchy</a>. A provisional government including the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alphonse-de-lamartine">Alphonse de Lamartine</a> proclaimed the Republic, introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/universal-suffrage">universal male suffrage</a>, abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the colonies under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-schoelcher">Victor Schoelcher's</a> decree, and created <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-workshops">National Workshops</a> for the unemployed.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The elected assembly was conservative, and the closure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-workshops">National Workshops</a> provoked the June Days uprising, crushed by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-eugene-cavaignac">Cavaignac</a> with thousands killed. In December 1848 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Louis-Napoléon Bonaparte</a>, nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, was elected president by a landslide. The assembly then restricted suffrage and passed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/falloux-laws">Falloux law</a> strengthening Church schools.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Barred from a second term, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Louis-Napoléon</a> staged a coup on 2 December 1851, approved by plebiscite. A year later, on 2 December 1852, he proclaimed himself Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> III, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-french-empire">Second French Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-second-republic.jpg" alt="French Second Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1848 CE – 1852 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Paris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alphonse de Lamartine, Louis-Eugène Cavaignac, Louis-Napoléon Bonaparte</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Second Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1850&amp;focus=french-second-republic" aria-label="French Second Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4734 472 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French Second Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5054 728h0M5054 728h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5054 728h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Paris. <a href="/atlas?year=1850&amp;focus=french-second-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
